<title>FRANCE: Paris June 97 export traffic up 1.3 pct says ADP.</title>
<headline>Paris June 97 export traffic up 1.3 pct says ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>June 1997 export airfreight traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 52,494 tonnes, an increase of 1.3 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports June 1997 export traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on June 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic		   3,346  down 11.0</p>
<p>    European Union	   5,857  up    0.6</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	    1,443  up   31.3</p>
<p>    North Africa		 949  up    6.5</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa     4,084  down  4.5</p>
<p>    North America	   15,277  down  1.3</p>
<p>    French territories     2,432  up    7.8</p>
<p>    Latin America	    3,109  up   15.8</p>
<p>    Middle East		4,839  down  1.9</p>
<p>    Far East		  11,158  up    5.1</p>
<p>    Total		     52,494  up    1.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
